            <ArticleTitle>Off-pump coronary bypass surgery for left main coronary artery stenosis 10 years after heart transplantation: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1178-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with asymptomatic left main coronary artery stenosis 10 years after heart transplantation was treated successfully with off-pump coronary bypass surgery using both mammary arteries. New advances in bypass surgery may decrease the risk of revascularization in cardiac transplant recipients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
